{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Effects tour: camera and graphics",
    "description": "Chapter 2 of the effects tour: every virtual camera preset over a bundled photograph (plus hits, seeded shake and keyframed zoom / roll), section motion (Ken Burns, pulse), letterbox, and every animated graphic: flash, bars, underline (round caps), frame (rounded, traced), corners (on a target), panel, wipe, glitch, focus, progress, ticker and bar chart.",
    "creativeDirection": "One camera idea or one graphic per beat, named in the corner label. Photographs make every camera move readable; graphics sit on ink grounds so their geometry reads. Review: no frame edge ever shows during a move, flashes stay under three per second, text keeps its shadow over photos, and the chart values settle before the cut."
  },
